<body>

<h1>Family Events CRUD, Pagination, Search & Role Permissions Architecture</h1>
<p><strong>Module:</strong> <code>FamilyEventsModule</code> (Backend)<br/>
<strong>Controller:</strong> <code>FamilyEventsController</code><br/>
<strong>Service:</strong> <code>FamilyEventsService</code><br/>
<strong>Base Route:</strong> <code>/family/events</code><br/>
<strong>Last Updated:</strong> September 25, 2026</p>

<div class="info-box">
    <strong>Executive Summary:</strong> The Family Events subsystem provides comprehensive lifecycle management for family gatherings, reunions, and virtual events. It features role-governed authorization (MEMBER, OWNER, ADMIN), query-driven server-side pagination and fuzzy search, single-item detail lookup, partial updates, and deletion.
</div>

<h2>1. Complete Endpoints Overview</h2>

<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Method</th>
            <th>Endpoint</th>
            <th>Role Permissions</th>
            <th>Purpose</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><span class="badge badge-get">GET</span></td>
            <td><code>/family/events</code></td>
            <td><code>[Roles: MEMBER, OWNER, ADMIN]</code></td>
            <td>List events with pagination (<code>page</code>, <code>limit</code>), search terms (<code>search</code>, <code>q</code>), virtual filter, sorting.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><span class="badge badge-post">POST</span></td>
            <td><code>/family/events</code></td>
            <td><code>[Roles: MEMBER, OWNER, ADMIN]</code></td>
            <td>Schedule a new family event with title, description, date/time, location, and virtual meeting details.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><span class="badge badge-get">GET</span></td>
            <td><code>/family/events/:id</code></td>
            <td><code>[Roles: MEMBER, OWNER, ADMIN]</code></td>
            <td>Retrieve complete details for a specific event by ID, scoped to user's family membership.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><span class="badge badge-patch">PATCH</span></td>
            <td><code>/family/events/:id</code></td>
            <td><code>[Roles: MEMBER, OWNER, ADMIN]</code></td>
            <td>Partially update an event (title, description, eventDate, location, isVirtual, meetingUrl).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><span class="badge badge-delete">DELETE</span></td>
            <td><code>/family/events/:id</code></td>
            <td><code>[Roles: OWNER, ADMIN]</code></td>
            <td>Permanently delete an event by ID (restricted to family Owners and Administrators).</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2>2. Pagination and Search Capabilities</h2>
<p>The <code>GET /family/events</code> endpoint accepts the following query parameters defined in <code>EventsQueryDto</code> extending <code>PaginationQueryDto</code>:</p>

<table>
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Parameter</th>
            <th>Type</th>
            <th>Default</th>
            <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td><code>page</code></td>
            <td>Integer</td>
            <td>1</td>
            <td>Current page number (1-indexed).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>limit</code></td>
            <td>Integer</td>
            <td>10</td>
            <td>Number of event records per page.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>search</code> / <code>q</code></td>
            <td>String</td>
            <td>null</td>
            <td>Fuzzy case-insensitive search matching event <code>title</code>, <code>description</code>, or <code>location</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>isVirtual</code></td>
            <td>Boolean</td>
            <td>null</td>
            <td>Optional filter for virtual/online events.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>status</code></td>
            <td>String</td>
            <td>null / "ALL"</td>
            <td>Filter events by status: <code>ACTIVE</code> (upcoming / scheduled on or after today) or <code>INACTIVE</code> (expired / past date).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>sortBy</code></td>
            <td>String</td>
            <td>"eventDate"</td>
            <td>Field to sort by (e.g. <code>eventDate</code>, <code>createdAt</code>, <code>title</code>).</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td><code>sortOrder</code></td>
            <td>String</td>
            <td>"asc"</td>
            <td>Sorting direction (<code>asc</code> or <code>desc</code>).</td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Event Lifecycle &amp; Status Auto-Calculation:</h3>
<div class="info-box">
  <strong>Dynamic Status Evaluation Rule:</strong>
  <ul>
    <li><code>ACTIVE</code>: Evaluated when <code>eventDate &gt;= today</code> (at midnight boundary). Indicates an upcoming or ongoing celebration scheduled for today or any future date.</li>
    <li><code>INACTIVE</code>: Evaluated when <code>eventDate &lt; today</code>. Indicates that the celebration date has passed and the event is expired.</li>
  </ul>
  Every single event returned by <code>getEvents</code>, <code>getEventById</code>, <code>createEvent</code>, and <code>updateEvent</code> is enriched with <code>status: 'ACTIVE' | 'INACTIVE'</code>.
</div>

<h3>Standard Paginated Response Envelope:</h3>
<pre>
{
  "statusCode": 200,
  "message": "Events retrieved successfully",
  "data": {
    "items": [
      {
        "id": "cm...event-id",
        "title": "Annual Summer Family Reunion",
        "description": "Potluck picnic, games, and family photo session.",
        "eventDate": "2026-10-15T10:00:00.000Z",
        "location": "Oak Tree Memorial Park, Pavilion 3",
        "isVirtual": false,
        "status": "ACTIVE",
        "familyId": "cm...family-id",
        "createdAt": "2026-09-25T08:00:00.000Z",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-25T08:00:00.000Z"
      }
    ],
    "meta": {
      "total": 1,
      "page": 1,
      "limit": 10,
      "totalPages": 1,
      "hasNextPage": false,
      "hasPreviousPage": false
    }
  }
}
</pre>

<h2>3. Single Event Detail (GET /family/events/:id)</h2>
<p>Allows authorized family members (MEMBER, OWNER, ADMIN) to inspect full metadata for an event. Performs family boundary validation to ensure members cannot access events belonging to another family sanctuary.</p>

<h2>4. Event Update (PATCH /family/events/:id)</h2>
<p>Accepts partial updates with full field validation via <code>UpdateEventDto</code>:</p>
<pre>
{
  "title"?: "Updated Reunion Title",
  "description"?: "Updated schedule and items to bring",
  "eventDate"?: "2026-07-15T11:00:00.000Z",
  "location"?: "Oak Tree Memorial Park, Main Pavilion",
  "isVirtual"?: false,
  "meetingUrl"?: null
}
</pre>

<h2>5. Event Deletion (DELETE /family/events/:id)</h2>
<p>Restricted to <code>OWNER</code> and <code>ADMIN</code> roles to safeguard schedule integrity. Ensures cascade safety and audit consistency within the family sanctuary.</p>

<h2>6. Swagger Documentation Integration</h2>
<p>All 5 endpoints are fully registered in the Swagger OpenApi Specification accessible at <code>/api/docs</code>. Role permission badges and explicit query parameters are visible directly in the interactive documentation interface.</p>

</body>
</html>
